A few notes on using this:

**Setup:** Open your spreadsheet, go to Extensions → Apps Script, paste the code, and save. Run `cleanVolunteerData` from the function dropdown. The first run will ask for permissions to read/write your spreadsheet.

**The CONFIG block** at the top is where you adjust behavior. Set `DEFAULT_AREA_CODE` to `""` if you'd rather flag 7-digit phones for review instead of guessing the area code. Change `DUP_WINDOW_MINUTES` to widen or narrow the name+timestamp clustering.

**What it writes:** The Clean sheet keeps all original columns (A–F) untouched on the left, then appends normalized columns and two flag columns. Green rows are ready to use, yellow need manual review, and red are superseded duplicates. The FlagNotes column tells you *why* a row was flagged, so you can filter on something like "Phone" to fix just the phone issues in bulk.

**Merge logic:** When two rows share a name and fall within the time window, the script keeps the later row and backfills any empty or REVIEW fields from the earlier one. This handles cases where someone resubmitted to fix a typo but left a field blank the second time.

**Idempotent:** You can re-run it safely. It clears and rebuilds the Clean sheet each time, so if you add new ParkMap entries or tweak CONFIG, just run it again.

